  "alternatives": [],
  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Medicaid Xiaflex (collagenase clostridium histolyticum), Version 1. Original 10/23/2019; Approval 11/15/2019; Effective 1/6/2020.",
    "Closed indication selections attest to confirmed Dupuytren’s contracture with a palpable cord or Peyronie’s disease in an adult man with a palpable plaque. Both paths require age ≥18. Failure to meet approval criteria is grounds for denial.",
    "Dupuytren’s two-vial requests (notes only): verify one cord affecting two joints in the same finger OR two cords affecting two joints in the same hand. Requested quantity and anatomical configuration require manual review.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval one treatment cycle; re-approval one treatment cycle. Dupuytren’s administration no sooner than 4 weeks, up to 3 cycles in total. Peyronie’s administration no sooner than 6 weeks with greater than 15 degree deformity, up to 4 cycles in total.",
    "Quantity limit (notes only): 2 vials (injections) per treatment cycle; no days-supply conversion is specified.",
    "Cautions (notes only): tendon rupture or serious injury to injected finger/hand; corporal rupture (penile fracture) or other serious penile injury. Contraindicated for Peyronie’s plaques involving the penile urethra. Use caution with abnormal anticoagulation.",
    "This pack remains partial: documentation verification, dual-vial anatomy, duration, reauthorization intervals and cycle totals, quantity enforcement and cautions require manual review."
  ],
